 {:id "adr-2607078000-kotoba-lang-wasm-webcomponent-cljs-esm-host"
  :title "ADR-2607078000: wasm-webcomponent's zero-build-step hand-JS host policy is superseded — kotoba/kototama WASM hosts are authored in ClojureScript, compiled once, run everywhere (browser + Node)"
  :status "accepted"
  :date "2026-07-07"
  :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"]
  :doc_type "adr"
  :topic "kotoba-lang-wasm-webcomponent-cljs-esm-host"
  :authoritative true
  :authoritative_for
  ["kotoba-lang/wasm-webcomponent: new policy -- kotoba/kototama WASM hosts needing more than a trivial hand-port are authored in ClojureScript and compiled via shadow-cljs :target :esm to a single ES module that runs identically in browser and Node, instead of hand-written per-platform JS. Existing hand-JS modules (actor-host.js/kgraph.js/has-capability.js/kotoba-wasm-element.js) are grandfathered, not retrofitted."
   "kotoba-lang/wasm-webcomponent src-cljs/kotoba/kami_engine_host.cljs (+ shadow-cljs.edn, compiled src/kami-engine-host.js, test/verify-kami-engine-host.mjs, examples/kami-engine-host/): first implementation under the new policy -- 1:1 port of kami-script-runtime-rs's HostState/EcsStore/KamiHost (14 kami:engine/* host-imports across 4 WASM import modules), parity-verified in Node against the real isekai-network-01-netsurvivors.wasm fixture for 300 ticks (entities=16 shiro-pico=1 ghost=14 beat-spark=1, exact match with kami-script-runtime-rs's own documented Rust/wasmtime trace)."
   "clojurewasm (cljw) ruled out for WASM-host-providing-imports roles: (1) native-binary-only, does not run in a browser; (2) its WebAssembly FFI is Clojure-calls-wasm only (wasm/load + wasm/call), no documented capability for cljw to provide host-import functions a guest wasm module calls into. Verified via its own README, not assumed."
   "Addendum 2026-07-08: direction widened to Rust-free including native/windowed targets, not just browser/Node. Concurrent-session work on kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime-rs (wasmi backend + kami_clj_play native winit+wgpu player) left untouched/unreverted (real, verified, another session's in-progress work), but a documentation-only org-direction notice was added to that crate's README.md/Cargo.toml (commit 4f08f5b42ae7bd4ac0ff91ab0e9c0f80e1b0c068) recording that native desktop targets should go through a webview/Chromium-shell wrapper around the same kami-engine-host/dom-gpu ClojureScript path going forward, not hand-written wgpu/winit. KamiHost's headless-host role (this ADR's actual replacement target, src/lib.rs) verified unaffected by the concurrent session's additions."
   "Addendum 2 (2026-07-08): Track A (kami-engine-host, removing kami-engine's Rust dependency) declared closed, no further action planned. Proceeding to Track B -- rendering kami-solar-helix-scene's solar helical model via guest-driven WebGPU, kotoba-wasm-runtime-first per CLAUDE.md's priority order, plan at ~/.claude/plans/curious-zooming-sifakis.md. Phase 0 (a synchronous-guest-driven-WebGPU-call technical-risk spike) is next."
   "Addendum 3 (2026-07-08): Track B Phase 0's capability-contract half landed -- gpu-clear(rgba8: i32) -> 0|-1 registered in kotoba-core-contracts (id 226, kotoba-core-contracts#5), one packed 0xRRGGBBAA i32 instead of the plan's sketched 3-param (r,g,b) shape (a deliberate ABI simplification during implementation, matching the (scalar-in) -> status-out convention every other non-buffer import here uses). NOT yet landed and NOT claimed as done: the actual browser host implementation (device/adapter/canvas setup + the gpu_clear HostFunction, authored in ClojureScript per this ADR's own Decision, not hand-JS), a minimal .kotoba guest, and Phase 0's real acceptance criterion -- a claude-in-chrome screenshot confirming the canvas genuinely clears to the requested color in a live browser tab. Phase 0 remains open until verified against a real browser, not just declared in an EDN table."
   "Addendum 4 (2026-07-08): Track B Phase 0 CLOSED, browser-verified. Addendum 3's outstanding half is now landed: kotoba-lang/wasm-webcomponent src-cljs/kotoba/gpu_clear_host.cljs -> src/gpu-clear-host.js (shadow-cljs :target :esm :advanced, ClojureScript-authored per this ADR's Decision, not hand-JS -- required unchecked-get/js-invoke throughout to survive :advanced property renaming against externs-less WebGPU calls) + demo_gpu_clear.kotoba (real kotoba wasm emit after bumping kotoba-lang/kotoba's kotoba-core-contracts pin to e5bc820 -- kotoba-lang/kotoba commit 3ba5f607, 146 tests/786 assertions green). Real browser verification via claude-in-chrome against GitHub Pages (https://kotoba-lang.github.io/wasm-webcomponent/examples/gpu-clear/, enabled specifically because both a local static server and a claude.ai Artifact iframe preview were unreachable/uninspectable from this sandboxed session): screenshot confirms canvas fully opaque red, #out reads 'main() -> 0 (0 = gpu_clear succeeded)'. Phase 0's actual risk -- guest-driven WebGPU as a genuinely synchronous host-import -- is confirmed against a live browser, not just argued from spec. Track B Phase 1 (cos/sin builtins, gpu-set-instance-transform/gpu-set-camera/gpu-draw-frame, kami-solar-helix-scene position-math port, 9-body vertical slice) is unblocked."
   "Addendum 5 (2026-07-08): proceeding to Track B Phase 1 -- .kotoba cos/sin builtins, gpu-set-instance-transform/gpu-set-camera/gpu-draw-frame capability set, kami-solar-helix-scene position-math port to .kotoba, 9-body (Sun + 8 planets) vertical-slice render with heliocentric/galactic frame toggle, browser-verified per Phase 0's precedent."]
